- /chevron\_sign\_right Loans and Loan Guarantees to support VPP projects with a focus on low- to moderate-income communities, including lowering the cost of financing for VPP-eligible DER;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Home Energy Rebates to reduce the cost of efficiency retrofits and electrification measures in homes and other buildings;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Weatherization Assistance Program for energy efficient and electric technologies in lowincome households, including improved insulation;

- /chevron\_sign\_right Technical Assistance for New and Stretch Code Adoption for adoption and enforcement of new and stretch building codes;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Energy Efficiency Grants for local governments, schools, and non-profits, including for deployment of DERs;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Energy Efficiency Loan Fund Capitalization Grants to support energy efficiency projects, including distributed solar;

- /chevron\_sign\_right Roadmap for deployment of Grid-interactive Efficient Buildings publication;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Connected Communities , a scaled demonstration of the technologies and approaches to VPP deployment;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Smart Grid Grants to increase the flexibility, efficiency, and reliability of the electric power system;
- /chevron\_sign\_right National EV Infrastructure Standards that ensure federally-funded charging equipment is capable of smart charging;

- /caret\_right Developing standard reference designs for the distribution grid to enable DERs utilization and orchestration;
- /caret\_right Developing guidelines on the staged deployment of foundational and co-dependent grid assets to enable the utilization and orchestration of DERs and incorporating them into planning guidelines for regulators;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Distributed Energy Resources Cybersecurity Risk Assessment and Mitigation report publication;

- /chevron\_sign\_right Distribution system cybersecurity baselines development as part of the National Cybersecurity Strategy, led by NARUC through DOE funding;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Cyber-Informed Engineering Strategy development for energy system architecture;
- /chevron\_sign\_right Energy Threat Analysis Center launch for cybersecurity threat collaboration between industry and government to enable collective defense;

- /caret\_right Testing at the National Renewable Energy Laboratory's Advanced Research on Integrated Energy Systems facilities for solar-plus-storage;
- /caret\_right Interconnection Innovation Exchange (I2X) and other programs for the development of interconnection standards for inverter-based resource and DERs to ensure system reliability;
- /caret\_right Cost-benefit analysis support for VPP solutions involving distributed solar and energy storage;

- /chevron\_sign\_right Clean Energy Innovator Fellowship funds recent graduates and energy professionals to support public utility commissions, co-ops, Puerto Rican energy associations, tribal utilities, and other grid operators;
- /chevron\_sign\_right State Energy Program provides funding and technical assistance to enhance energy security, advance state-led initiatives, and increase energy affordability;
- /chevron\_sign\_right DER Compensation Initiative to engage regulators via a cooperative agreement with the National Association of Regulatory Utility Commissioners.
